{
  "summary": "Updates the legacy-to-SQLite wallet migration process to skip copying legacy records and transaction records upfront rather than copying and subsequently erasing them. Because migration generates replacement descriptor records and rewrites transactions anyway, filtering these record types during MigrateToSQLite avoids redundant database writes. Removing the post-migration deletion steps allows dropping unused database erase functions (EraseTx, RemoveTxs, DeleteRecordsWithDB, EraseRecords) and scoping HasLegacyRecords as static to walletdb.cpp.",
  "problem": "Legacy wallet migration dumps all BDB records into a new SQLite database, only for subsequent steps to immediately erase legacy key and script records and delete or rewrite transaction records. This incurs unnecessary disk I/O during migration and requires maintaining dead record-erasure code paths in the wallet.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'The legacy wallet records are replaced with descriptor records produced during migration, and transaction records are already being rewritten by migration, so not writing them in the first place is also fine. This allows us to remove several database record erase functions, specifically EraseTx and EraseRecords.'"
  ],
